WEBVTT

00:00:06.980 --> 00:00:09.980
This is a work of fiction based on research into the period in which it is set. The people,
 organization, laws, and names that appear in it have no relation to any in the real world.

00:01:39.990 --> 00:01:45.000
The Letter

00:02:10.940 --> 00:02:14.320
Speak again, Jokanaan.

00:02:14.320 --> 00:02:17.320
Speak again, Jokanaan.

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:17.400
One year ago, winter
Tokyo Station

00:02:40.100 --> 00:02:41.680
It's like a cloud.

00:02:44.730 --> 00:02:46.690
Umm, excuse me.

00:02:46.690 --> 00:02:48.190
What is it?

00:02:48.190 --> 00:02:50.730
Where is the Imperial Theater?

00:02:52.400 --> 00:02:55.240
Are you really fine with the attic?

00:02:55.240 --> 00:02:58.910
You do have an introduction
from Mr. Okimura.

00:02:58.910 --> 00:03:01.080
I requested it.

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:03.040
I don't mind the attic.

00:03:27.560 --> 00:03:31.730
So, this will be my home from now on.

00:03:31.730 --> 00:03:33.980
This is my place.

00:03:36.740 --> 00:03:38.490
A mouse?

00:03:38.490 --> 00:03:40.070
Not there.

00:03:41.410 --> 00:03:43.330
A ghost?

00:03:43.330 --> 00:03:44.950
Leave.

00:03:45.950 --> 00:03:48.370
How did you get in here?

00:03:48.370 --> 00:03:52.880
I won't tell anyone,
but you should leave quickly.

00:03:52.880 --> 00:03:55.920
Are you listening to me?

00:03:55.920 --> 00:03:58.180
Oh, my, you're so thin!

00:03:58.180 --> 00:04:00.140
Are you eating enough?

00:04:00.140 --> 00:04:01.760
Are you hungry?

00:04:01.760 --> 00:04:03.220
You talk too much.

00:04:03.220 --> 00:04:06.020
Would you not point the lamp
at me? It's blinding.

00:04:06.020 --> 00:04:08.520
Oh, I'm sorry.

00:04:08.520 --> 00:04:10.440
But I'm worried for you.

00:04:13.400 --> 00:04:14.610
Please,

00:04:14.610 --> 00:04:16.490
leave me alone.

00:04:16.490 --> 00:04:18.570
Where are you going?

00:04:18.570 --> 00:04:20.860
It's time.

00:04:20.860 --> 00:04:22.240
Time for what?

00:04:25.330 --> 00:04:28.460
This is a tale of long ago.

00:04:28.460 --> 00:04:35.340
I, Defrott, play a devil who dwells
in a dark forest in far-off Russia.

00:04:35.340 --> 00:04:39.260
Then, a tired soldier on his way home

00:04:39.260 --> 00:04:42.340
walks into the forest,
violin in one hand.

00:04:40.510 --> 00:04:42.340
Isn't Defrott a marvel?

00:04:42.340 --> 00:04:47.060
Though he is exhausted,
his footsteps are light,

00:04:43.220 --> 00:04:45.140
Umm, who is he?

00:04:45.140 --> 00:04:50.600
He was a child actor in England.
The British ambassador recommended him.

00:04:47.060 --> 00:04:50.600
and his mud-spattered face
is grinning from ear to ear.

00:04:50.600 --> 00:04:52.900
I had no idea he was so amazing.

00:05:10.500 --> 00:05:13.170
Welcome home, Defrott.

00:05:13.170 --> 00:05:15.460
You're still here.

00:05:15.460 --> 00:05:19.340
The manager told me about you, Defrott.

00:05:21.220 --> 00:05:25.680
I'm amazed. You've been acting
ever since you were little.

00:05:38.820 --> 00:05:39.740
What?

00:05:39.740 --> 00:05:42.860
I'm Misaki Nakajima.

00:05:42.860 --> 00:05:45.530
Pleased to meet you.

00:05:45.530 --> 00:05:47.990
Would you leave me alone?

00:05:47.990 --> 00:05:52.790
But I'm a performer here, too,
so we might be in a play together.

00:05:52.790 --> 00:05:56.380
That doesn't mean we have to be friends.

00:06:05.090 --> 00:06:07.220
It's crooked.

00:06:07.220 --> 00:06:10.350
I knew I wouldn't look good in this.

00:06:10.350 --> 00:06:13.690
Weren't you the one who said
you'd join the army?

00:06:13.690 --> 00:06:15.850
That's true, but...

00:06:15.850 --> 00:06:19.440
You could have just kept
freeloading at our place.

00:06:19.440 --> 00:06:21.740
I told you, I can't.

00:06:21.740 --> 00:06:26.910
I've been staying at your house
ever since we lost our draper's shop.

00:06:26.910 --> 00:06:30.080
I can't presume on your kindness any...

00:06:30.080 --> 00:06:31.910
We don't mind.

00:06:31.910 --> 00:06:35.120
Since my big brother Sentaro died,

00:06:35.120 --> 00:06:39.840
Mom's taken care of you
like you're her own son.

00:06:39.840 --> 00:06:42.590
But... I'm grow up now.

00:06:42.590 --> 00:06:45.380
I've got to be independent. Besides--

00:06:45.380 --> 00:06:48.890
Do you hate people assuming
you're my fiancé that much?

00:06:48.890 --> 00:06:50.470
That's not...

00:06:50.470 --> 00:06:52.520
You let rumors bother you too much!

00:06:52.520 --> 00:06:54.310
That's not it.

00:06:54.310 --> 00:06:57.350
What is it? Just say it.

00:06:58.560 --> 00:07:00.690
You're so strong, Aoi.

00:07:00.690 --> 00:07:03.110
What's that mean?

00:07:03.110 --> 00:07:05.280
Even when Sentaro died,

00:07:05.280 --> 00:07:08.620
you tried not to shed a tear.

00:07:08.620 --> 00:07:12.240
I'm always just a crybaby.

00:07:12.240 --> 00:07:14.910
So, I want to get stronger.

00:07:18.500 --> 00:07:19.330
Ow!

00:07:19.330 --> 00:07:20.840
Promise me!

00:07:20.840 --> 00:07:21.670
Huh?

00:07:21.670 --> 00:07:25.380
Promise me that at least
you won't die, Shutaro.

00:07:31.140 --> 00:07:33.470
Okay, I promise.

00:07:35.270 --> 00:07:36.940
Great!

00:07:36.940 --> 00:07:40.060
Go to Siberia or wherever
and come back home!

00:07:40.060 --> 00:07:41.150
Yes, ma'am!

00:07:49.490 --> 00:07:51.580
May you arrive safely.

00:07:58.120 --> 00:07:59.630
Thank you all.

00:08:03.250 --> 00:08:05.340
Here.

00:08:05.340 --> 00:08:06.800
Siberia cake.

00:08:06.800 --> 00:08:09.090
You'll collapse if you don't eat.

00:08:11.430 --> 00:08:13.310
I don't need it.

00:08:13.310 --> 00:08:15.930
That would never suit my palate.

00:08:15.930 --> 00:08:17.810
Stop complaining and eat!

00:08:19.810 --> 00:08:21.520
I'll eat it later.

00:08:21.520 --> 00:08:23.320
You'd better eat it!

00:08:25.070 --> 00:08:26.900
Is that Shakespeare?

00:08:26.900 --> 00:08:28.530
<i>Romeo and Juliet.</i>

00:08:28.530 --> 00:08:31.780
Wow! Are you playing Romeo?

00:08:31.780 --> 00:08:32.910
Yes,

00:08:32.910 --> 00:08:37.450
but I hear they haven't found
a fitting actress for Juliet yet.

00:08:37.450 --> 00:08:41.250
At this rate, it will be my one-man show.

00:08:41.250 --> 00:08:42.840
I see.

00:08:42.840 --> 00:08:46.000
You're angling for the lead
in <i>Salomé</i>, aren't you?

00:08:46.000 --> 00:08:48.550
I am!

00:08:48.550 --> 00:08:52.090
How good to see the moon!

00:08:52.090 --> 00:08:55.060
She is like a little piece of money,

00:08:55.060 --> 00:08:57.770
a little silver flower.

00:08:57.770 --> 00:09:00.850
She is cold and chaste.

00:09:00.850 --> 00:09:04.110
I am sure she is a virgin.

00:09:04.110 --> 00:09:06.820
The Lord hath come.

00:09:06.820 --> 00:09:09.450
The son of man hath come.

00:09:11.200 --> 00:09:12.410
What?

00:09:12.410 --> 00:09:14.780
Why do you know the lines?

00:09:14.780 --> 00:09:17.790
Well, I'm a live-in actor here.

00:09:17.790 --> 00:09:21.120
I have to stand in if anything happens.

00:09:21.120 --> 00:09:25.130
And your Salomé is straight
out of some threepenny play.

00:09:25.130 --> 00:09:29.260
Who do you think you are
to give me direction?

00:09:30.970 --> 00:09:32.590
A princess.

00:09:32.590 --> 00:09:35.890
Real princesses don't pretend.

00:09:35.890 --> 00:09:41.140
They don't play princesses;
they <i>are </i>princesses.

00:09:41.140 --> 00:09:44.190
You make it sound like
you've met real princesses.

00:09:44.190 --> 00:09:45.860
Because I have.

00:09:45.860 --> 00:09:49.940
Wow! That's amazing, Defrott!

00:09:49.940 --> 00:09:52.860
Would you not treat me like a child?

00:09:52.860 --> 00:09:56.410
I've been acting longer than you have.

00:09:56.410 --> 00:09:59.200
All right, Defrott, sir.

00:09:59.200 --> 00:10:01.040
"Sir"?

00:10:01.040 --> 00:10:04.420
What should I do to become Salomé?

00:10:09.800 --> 00:10:14.180
How good to see the moon!

00:10:14.180 --> 00:10:17.720
She is like a little piece of money,

00:10:17.720 --> 00:10:20.850
a little silver flower.

00:10:20.850 --> 00:10:23.690
She is cold and chaste.

00:10:23.690 --> 00:10:28.020
I am sure she is a virgin.

00:10:28.020 --> 00:10:29.900
Wow.

00:10:29.900 --> 00:10:31.650
You nailed it.

00:10:31.650 --> 00:10:37.370
Your performance is merely someone's
painting of a princess called Salomé.

00:10:37.370 --> 00:10:40.790
You play her knowing how the story ends.

00:10:40.790 --> 00:10:42.450
So, it rings false.

00:10:42.450 --> 00:10:48.790
You don't yet know that your love
is bloody and cursed.

00:10:48.790 --> 00:10:52.130
You believe that your love is pure.

00:10:53.130 --> 00:10:55.090
Now, once more!

00:11:02.680 --> 00:11:06.770
How good to see the moon!

00:11:06.770 --> 00:11:10.980
She is like a little piece of money,

00:11:10.980 --> 00:11:13.740
a little silver flower.

00:11:13.740 --> 00:11:17.360
She is cold and chaste.

00:11:17.360 --> 00:11:21.030
I am sure she is a virgin.

00:11:41.260 --> 00:11:42.770
Misaki!

00:11:43.890 --> 00:11:45.680
Oh, my, Mr. Okimura!

00:11:45.680 --> 00:11:49.810
I hear you'll play the lead
in the next play.

00:11:49.810 --> 00:11:52.230
Yes! I'll play Salomé!

00:11:52.230 --> 00:11:56.070
Oh, is that... Oscar Wilde?

00:11:56.070 --> 00:11:57.990
I'm impressed you know it.

00:11:57.990 --> 00:12:00.820
Will Nakajima come to watch?

00:12:00.820 --> 00:12:04.290
My father is... busy with his work.

00:12:04.290 --> 00:12:06.210
That won't do!

00:12:06.210 --> 00:12:11.170
We can't deepen our relations
with Britain without cultural exchange.

00:12:11.170 --> 00:12:13.960
How can he be so dismissive?

00:12:13.960 --> 00:12:17.720
I know! I'll talk to him about it myself.

00:12:17.720 --> 00:12:20.260
I'm awfully sorry.

00:12:20.260 --> 00:12:24.100
You helped me so much when
I joined the Imperial Theater, too.

00:12:24.100 --> 00:12:26.770
Oh, don't mention it.

00:12:26.770 --> 00:12:30.270
Besides, I see him all the time.

00:12:30.270 --> 00:12:33.150
Well, I'll be looking forward to it.

00:12:33.150 --> 00:12:34.730
Thank you very much.

00:12:38.400 --> 00:12:42.410
Would you like some cake, Defrott?

00:12:42.410 --> 00:12:47.580
Are you <i>trying </i>to bother me?

00:12:47.580 --> 00:12:50.120
I'm joking.

00:12:50.120 --> 00:12:52.750
Where have you been?

00:12:52.750 --> 00:12:53.920
My house.

00:12:53.920 --> 00:12:58.720
Oh, it's close enough for you to go
in the morning and get back now?

00:12:58.720 --> 00:13:02.890
Yes. It's in Hikawacho in Akasaka.

00:13:02.890 --> 00:13:05.260
Then you should commute from there.

00:13:07.270 --> 00:13:10.640
That place... scares me.

00:13:10.640 --> 00:13:13.020
Don't you have family?

00:13:13.020 --> 00:13:15.610
I have my father,

00:13:15.610 --> 00:13:19.700
but he's busy with work and never at home.

00:13:19.700 --> 00:13:25.410
So, I only go there occasionally
to get fresh clothes and letters.

00:13:25.410 --> 00:13:28.660
This is my home now.

00:13:28.660 --> 00:13:30.540
I see.

00:13:30.540 --> 00:13:33.710
So, is that one of those letters?

00:13:33.710 --> 00:13:35.500
Well,

00:13:35.500 --> 00:13:37.710
it's a letter from Mr. Maeda.

00:13:37.710 --> 00:13:39.550
He's a friend of my father's.

00:13:39.550 --> 00:13:42.510
Hmm. What's he like?

00:13:42.510 --> 00:13:45.100
He's my fiancé,

00:13:45.100 --> 00:13:47.390
but we've never met.

00:13:47.390 --> 00:13:48.560
What?!

00:13:48.560 --> 00:13:50.270
He only writes.

00:13:50.270 --> 00:13:52.140
Still,

00:13:52.140 --> 00:13:56.270
his letters are always short, but there's
something tasteful about them.

00:13:56.270 --> 00:13:58.150
They're sensitive.

00:13:58.150 --> 00:14:00.650
There was a pressed flower
in the last one!

00:14:00.650 --> 00:14:03.910
It's fine. I don't want to look
at other people's letters.

00:14:03.910 --> 00:14:05.070
Here it is!

00:14:05.070 --> 00:14:07.080
Look! White clover!

00:14:08.700 --> 00:14:10.950
That's just a weed.

00:14:10.950 --> 00:14:13.210
I like it! Isn't it cute?

00:14:13.210 --> 00:14:14.330
It's strange.

00:14:14.330 --> 00:14:18.000
Marrying a man you've never even seen?

00:14:18.000 --> 00:14:20.460
It's like the 16th century.

00:14:20.460 --> 00:14:24.050
Do you think so? It's normal in Japan.

00:14:24.130 --> 00:14:29.640
Ms. Misaki Nakajima

00:14:25.140 --> 00:14:29.720
When I read his letters,
even without meeting him, I can tell.

00:14:29.720 --> 00:14:34.600
He's very kind and strong... and shy.

00:14:34.600 --> 00:14:37.560
It's like Cyrano de Bergerac.

00:14:37.560 --> 00:14:39.110
What's that?

00:14:39.110 --> 00:14:43.610
A story about falling in love
just by reading letters.

00:14:43.610 --> 00:14:45.490
How does it end?

00:14:49.200 --> 00:14:50.790
It's a tragedy.

00:14:54.990 --> 00:15:00.120
"Imperial Theater
<i>Salomé</i>"

00:14:56.420 --> 00:15:00.300
I can't believe something like this
is popular with modern girls.

00:15:00.300 --> 00:15:02.840
Isn't the subject classical?

00:15:02.840 --> 00:15:06.340
What's supposed to be fresh about that?

00:15:06.340 --> 00:15:09.050
I wouldn't be here if it weren't for work.

00:15:14.440 --> 00:15:18.610
So, Salomé is a newcomer
in her first starring role.

00:15:14.510 --> 00:15:18.270
Lead:
Misaki
Nakajima

00:15:14.510 --> 00:15:18.270
Young
genius

00:15:18.610 --> 00:15:22.650
I wonder if I'll be able to
stay awake all the way through.

00:15:28.740 --> 00:15:32.580
I'm telling you; this Salomé is amazing!

00:15:32.580 --> 00:15:34.960
First, the lead, Misaki, is amazing!

00:15:34.960 --> 00:15:37.290
That performance! She <i>is </i>Princess Salomé!

00:15:37.290 --> 00:15:39.710
A fresh interpretation,
but played flawlessly!

00:15:39.710 --> 00:15:43.550
The staging, lighting, music,
and set dressing are all amazing, too!

00:15:43.550 --> 00:15:46.260
How many "amazings" does that make?

00:15:46.260 --> 00:15:47.970
Anyway, it's amazing!

00:15:47.970 --> 00:15:50.930
Let me do a piece on the next play,
<i>Romeo and Juliet</i>, too!

00:15:50.930 --> 00:15:53.850
Misaki, who played Salomé,
is playing Juliet!

00:15:53.850 --> 00:15:56.690
And I'm sure Romeo will be lovely, too!

00:15:56.690 --> 00:16:00.650
I mean, the boy playing him
has blonde hair! Blonde!

00:16:00.650 --> 00:16:05.030
The Imperial Theater, huh?
I don't have many connections there.

00:16:05.030 --> 00:16:07.570
The flappers are clamoring for it!

00:16:16.790 --> 00:16:19.080
Welcome home.

00:16:19.080 --> 00:16:21.380
So, you're back.

00:16:22.380 --> 00:16:24.250
I am.

00:16:24.250 --> 00:16:27.720
Things will be busy
at the Imperial Theater,

00:16:27.720 --> 00:16:31.010
so I wanted to see to things at home.

00:16:38.480 --> 00:16:41.440
You cut your hair?

00:16:41.440 --> 00:16:44.570
This is my resolve.

00:16:44.570 --> 00:16:46.820
Doesn't it suit me?

00:16:46.820 --> 00:16:48.570
It does.

00:16:48.570 --> 00:16:51.280
Okimura told me.

00:16:51.280 --> 00:16:54.080
Congratulations on the lead.

00:16:54.080 --> 00:16:55.660
Thank you very much.

00:16:58.620 --> 00:17:03.750
Oh, yes, I hear Maeda is coming back.

00:17:03.750 --> 00:17:04.800
Mr. Maeda is?!

00:17:04.800 --> 00:17:07.050
How are his injuries?

00:17:07.050 --> 00:17:10.430
I hear he's feeling much better.

00:17:11.430 --> 00:17:15.470
Mr. Maeda... can come back.

00:17:20.020 --> 00:17:24.940
Dear Mr. Maeda,
please accept these few lines.

00:17:24.940 --> 00:17:30.820
It's now the season when sunflowers
stand out beautifully against blue skies.

00:17:30.820 --> 00:17:32.990
How have you been?

00:17:45.790 --> 00:17:48.920
I thought I told you not to come here.

00:17:48.920 --> 00:17:52.720
And here I've brought you
S blood from Yokohama.

00:17:52.720 --> 00:17:54.680
Oh?

00:17:54.680 --> 00:17:57.560
That is a pleasant surprise.

00:17:57.560 --> 00:18:00.230
It still requires adjustments.

00:18:00.230 --> 00:18:05.110
I prepared it because it's needed
for the transaction with Mr. Okimura.

00:18:05.110 --> 00:18:08.320
There were a few sacrifices, but...

00:18:08.320 --> 00:18:14.280
The path we walk is a dark road
through the night.

00:18:18.290 --> 00:18:19.950
Father.

00:18:23.290 --> 00:18:25.460
How careless.

00:18:35.390 --> 00:18:39.720
Is something wrong, miss?

00:18:39.720 --> 00:18:44.850
You look like you've
been possessed by a devil.

00:18:44.850 --> 00:18:47.520
A devil...

00:18:47.520 --> 00:18:49.730
You may be right.

00:18:51.110 --> 00:18:53.860
Defrott,

00:18:53.860 --> 00:18:57.660
do you think that vampires are real?

00:19:00.160 --> 00:19:02.700
Why do you want to know?

00:19:02.700 --> 00:19:05.250
My father...

00:19:05.250 --> 00:19:08.090
No, it's nothing.

00:19:10.300 --> 00:19:12.170
I'll go rehearse on stage.

00:19:28.520 --> 00:19:32.320
How good to see the moon!

00:19:32.320 --> 00:19:35.900
She is like a little piece of money,

00:19:35.900 --> 00:19:39.620
a little silver flower.

00:19:39.620 --> 00:19:42.750
She is cold and chaste.

00:19:42.750 --> 00:19:46.000
I am sure she is a virgin.

00:19:47.420 --> 00:19:52.590
To kiss thy mouth, my lips
to thy lips, my words to thy words.

00:19:52.590 --> 00:19:57.300
It is thy mouth that I desire, Jokanaan.

00:19:57.300 --> 00:20:01.260
Bring forth this prophet.

00:20:06.890 --> 00:20:07.940
Call a doctor!

00:20:07.940 --> 00:20:09.520
Salomé's pinned under it!

00:20:09.520 --> 00:20:10.650
Can you move it?!

00:20:10.650 --> 00:20:12.570
We'd need more people!

00:20:17.910 --> 00:20:19.530
Miss...

00:20:21.700 --> 00:20:24.290
I-I have to apologize.

00:20:28.370 --> 00:20:34.960
I want to show Mr. Maeda...
my Salomé, but...

00:20:38.880 --> 00:20:41.550
I'm sure you'll be all right, miss.

00:20:43.680 --> 00:20:45.060
So...

00:21:08.910 --> 00:21:11.960
Take her to Tsukishima Island.

00:21:17.460 --> 00:21:23.800
Speak again,

00:21:23.800 --> 00:21:25.640
Jokanaan.

00:21:31.810 --> 00:21:36.190
Weren't you going to keep
your promise to Misaki?

00:21:38.070 --> 00:21:43.530
At least put an end to
what you started yourselves!

00:21:43.530 --> 00:21:45.450
Get up, human.

00:21:48.080 --> 00:21:52.620
I won't let you leave the stage
having stained our twilight years.

